[center][size=6][b]RADIANCE[/b][/size]
[size=4][color=#e8c882]P L A Y E R   L I G H T   S O U R C E[/color][/size]

[size=3]Too dark to see? Light your way without holding a torch.[/size]

[b]Client side only.[/b] Install it on your own game; the server needs nothing.[/center]

[center][b]More mods by GreeneyeDS:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/220]The Worst Map Mod[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/195]Quick Deposit[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/200]Find[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/219]Embervale Teleport[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/255]Town Portals[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/272]Hollow Halls Progression[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/197]Continue[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/384/384-1795122870-1326222631.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]

Nights in Embervale are dark, and caves are darker. A torch fixes that, but it takes a hand you want for a shield, a bow or a pickaxe. Radiance makes your character give off light, so both hands stay free.
[list]
[*][b]A Wax Torch's light, hands free.[/b] The default matches a Wax Torch you hold: the same warm color, brightness and reach.
[*][b]No item, no crafting, no slot.[/b] Nothing goes in your backpack, and nothing is added to the game's items.
[*][b]F8 turns the light on or off.[/b]
[*][b]Shift+F8 opens a small menu[/b], drawn with the game's own interface: a switch, Brightness, Range and nine colors. Use it with the mouse. Esc or Close when you are done.
[*][b]Brightness up to three times a torch, range up to 300 m.[/b] Light a whole cave, or keep a small glow around your feet.
[*][b]Works on any server, with nothing installed on it.[/b] The light is on your own game.
[*][b]Other players with Radiance see your light, and you see theirs[/b] (see Multiplayer below).
[*][b]In your language:[/b] the menu follows the game's language setting, in all 15 languages Enshrouded supports.
[*][b]Controller support:[/b] hold LB and press D-pad Left for the menu; the D-pad moves through it, A flips the switch, B closes.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/384/384-1795122884-1123101727.jpg[/img]

[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/384/384-1795379901-991733545.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Close Enshrouded.
[*]Open the game folder (Steam: right-click Enshrouded > Manage > Browse local files).
[*]Copy everything from the zip into it, keeping the folders: [b]dbgcore.dll[/b] next to [i]enshrouded.exe[/i], and the [b]greeneye\radiance[/b] folder.
[*]Start the game and load into a world. The light is on; [b]F8[/b] turns it off and on, [b]Shift+F8[/b] opens the menu.
[/list]

[b]Client side only:[/b] that's all, for single player, hosted games and dedicated servers alike. Nothing goes on the server.

[b]Install by hand:[/b] Vortex does not know the Greeneye Loader yet.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [i]greeneye\radiance[/i]; if no other Greeneye mod is left, also [i]dbgcore.dll[/i] and the [i]greeneye[/i] folder.

[line]

[size=4][b]Multiplayer[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Players with Radiance[/b] see each other's lights, in each player's own color, brightness and range. The mods find each other through the game's chat channel, so the server needs nothing.
[*][b]Players without Radiance[/b] see one empty chat message when you join a world (the hello the mods find each other with); nothing more is sent unless another Radiance player is there. Your light is drawn by your game only.
[*][b]Your choice:[/b] [i]ShareMyLight[/i] and [i]ShowOtherLights[/i] in the settings file turn each direction off.
[*]A light shows on a player once they are in view.
[/list]

Seeing each other's lights is new and has only been tested by one player so far. If it works for your group, or doesn't, please say so in the comments.

[line]

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]

The menu covers the everyday choices. Everything else is in [i]greeneye\radiance\radiance.ini[/i], each setting explained in the file. Changes apply within a second of saving it; no restart needed. What you change in the menu is written to the same file.
[list]
[*][b]Enabled[/b], [b]Intensity[/b], [b]Radius[/b]: the menu's switch, Brightness and Range. Intensity 1 and Radius 45 are a Wax Torch.
[*][b]Color[/b] = 255, 137, 88: any color, as red, green, blue from 0 to 255 or a web color such as [i]#FF8958[/i]. The menu offers nine.
[*][b]Flicker[/b] = 1.0: how fast the light flickers. 0 is a steady light.
[*][b]Height[/b] = 1.3: where the light sits, in metres above your feet.
[*][b]Shadows[/b] = false: [i]true[/i] makes the light cast shadows. Costs some frame rate.
[*][b]ShareMyLight[/b] and [b]ShowOtherLights[/b]: see Multiplayer.
[*][b]ToggleLight[/b] = F8 and [b]OpenMenu[/b] = Shift+F8, Pad:LB+Left: the keys. Any key with Shift+, Ctrl+ or Alt+ in front; a controller button goes after a comma.
[*][b]Language[/b] = auto: the menu's language, if you want another than the game's.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Languages[/b][/size]

The menu comes in every language the game supports: English, French, Italian, German, Spanish, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Portuguese (Brazil), Russian, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Turkish, Ukrainian and Thai. It follows the language set in the game, and uses the game's own words for On, Off, Brightness and Close.

The translations were made with AI. If a word reads oddly in your language, please post a better one in the comments.

[line]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Single player, hosted games and dedicated servers.[/b] Client side only: it changes nothing on the server and nothing in your save.
[*][b]No new items.[/b] The light is one of the game's own light effects, placed at your character. Remove the mod and nothing is left behind.
[*][b]Plays well with other mods.[/b] It runs through the Greeneye Loader ([i]dbgcore.dll[/i], shared with Find, Quick Deposit, Embervale Teleport, Town Portals, Hollow Halls Progression and The Worst Map Mod), and chains onto hooks other mods put on the same game functions.
[*][b]Safe on game updates.[/b] Made for the current game version. The mod finds what it needs in the game when it starts; if an update changes that, it switches the affected part off (the menu, the shared lights, or the light itself) instead of risking a crash, and says so in [i]greeneye\loader.log[/i].
[*]Your character's back can look dark from behind: the light sits inside the body at chest height, like a lantern on your belt. [i]Height[/i] in the settings moves it.
[*]Works with Steam on Windows. Not tested with other store versions, or on Linux / Steam Deck.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

If something doesn't work, please post this with your report:
[list]
[*][i]greeneye\loader.log[/i] in the game folder: what the Greeneye Loader and the mod did (the mod's lines start with "Radiance:").
[*]Your [i]greeneye\radiance\radiance.ini[/i], if the light looks wrong.
[/list]

No light at all? Check that [i]dbgcore.dll[/i] sits next to [i]enshrouded.exe[/i], that [i]Enabled=true[/i] is in the settings file, and press F8 once.

[line]

[size=4][b]Changelog[/b][/size]

[b]1.1.0[/b]
[list]
[*]The menu looks like the game's own dialogs: the framed window Find's search uses, the game's stone Close button, and slider rows laid out like the game's Settings screen.
[*]Far fewer hidden chat lines: players without Radiance saw an empty chat message every 10 seconds. Now one is sent when you join a world, and nothing more unless another Radiance player is there.
[*]Safer on game updates: more of what the mod uses is read from the game at start; if a menu piece changes in an update, the menu draws its own instead.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]Empty chat messages for players without the mod (Neocybermario).
[/list]

[b]1.0.0[/b]
[list]
[*]First release.
[/list]

